WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:01.425
Why three questions?

2
00:00:01.425 --> 00:00:05.503
Because a private endpoint that exists
can still go unused if the name

3
00:00:05.503 --> 00:00:09.863
doesn't resolve to it, and can still be
bypassed if the public path stays open.

4
00:00:09.863 --> 00:00:12.819
By the end of this chapter
you can answer four things:

5
00:00:12.819 --> 00:00:16.463
whether every privatelink zone is
central and linked to the hub,

6
00:00:16.463 --> 00:00:20.519
whether every private endpoint
registers its record in a central zone,

7
00:00:20.519 --> 00:00:24.438
which resources still accept public
traffic beside their endpoint,

8
00:00:24.438 --> 00:00:28.838
and which key vaults miss any part of
the posture Microsoft Learn recommends.

9
00:00:28.838 --> 00:00:31.525
And you can compute the
guide's vault-posture metric.

10
00:00:31.525 --> 00:00:35.303
It's for platform owners, who
own the zones; workload owners,

11
00:00:35.303 --> 00:00:39.530
who own endpoints and vaults; and
the developers who review both.
